    "billPage": 0,
    "chapter": 0,
    "lineEnd": 0,
    "lineStart": 0,
    "memoText": "\n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 207\n\nTO THE ASSEMBLY:\n\nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n\nAssembly Bill Number 6575, entitled:\n\n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend  the  tax  law,  in  relation to providing for a\n      deduction from personal gross income for expenses incurred in  the\n      adoption of a child in the foster care system\"\n\n    NOT APPROVED\n\n  This  bill  would  provide  a deduction from personal gross income for\nexpenses incurred in adopting a child in the foster care system.\n\n  I vetoed identical legislation last year (Veto Memo No. 556 of  2014).\nWhile  I  fully  support  the underlying goals of this legislation, this\nbill is overly broad and  would  unnecessarily  duplicate  existing  tax\nbenefits  available  to  families  that  adopt  children. New York State\nalready provides subsidies to cover expenses related to the adoption  of\nhard-to-place  children  and monthly payments to the parents of children\nwho adopt from the foster care system. Further, children adopted out  of\nthe  foster care system are universally eligible for Medicaid. This bill\nwould also impose a  cost  to  the  State  that  is  more  appropriately\ndiscussed  in  the  context of the State budget. As a result, I am again\nconstrained to veto this bill.\n\n  The bill is disapproved.                    (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n\n                               __________\n",
    "signedDate": null,
    "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
    "vetoNumber": 207,
    "vetoType": "STANDARD",
    "year": 2015
   }
